content.text:
Now Part 2 & 3 in ps5.js — the big piece.

**GAMES expansion to 10 unique games.** I need to keep `gta` entry (existing) and add 9 new unique games. Each unique: title, sub, colors, hours, progress, rating, installed, owned, price, story, character, city, music, control, missions count, mode.

Then `launchGame` should open only that game. And per-game save key via `this.currentGameId`.

Let me write the new GAMES array. Keep existing 6 and add 4? No — user wants 10 total including GTA BR. Existing list has 6 (gta, cidade, favela, corrida, futebol, moto). I need GTA BR + 9 others = 10. The user listed specific 10:
1. GTA BR
2. FIFA BR
3. GOD OF WAR BR
4. SPIDER-MAN BR
5. FREE FIRE BR
6. MINECRAFT BR
7. FORZA BR
8. THE LAST OF US BR
9. FORTNITE BR
10. CALL OF DUTY BR

So I should replace/restructure the GAMES list to these 10. The existing entries like 'cidade' (CAIO: A CIDADE) etc. don't match the requested 10; better to build the requested 10 exactly, keeping GTA BR entry as the playable one and owned/installed states sensible.

Design GAMES entries with unique fields:

```js
const GAMES = [
  { id: 'gta', title: 'GTA 5 BR', sub: 'Edição Caio · Mundo aberto brasileiro', c1: '#ff7a18', c2: '#56118d', c3: '#ffc32b', hours: 248, progress: 87, rating: '18+', installed: true, owned: true, price: 349.9, story: 'Caio monta o império do crime na Cidade Caio.', character: 'CAIO BR', city: 'São Paulo · RP', music: 'funk', control: 'GTA', missions: 50, mode: 'open' },
  { id: 'fifa', title: 'FIFA BR', sub: 'Campeonato da América · Seleção Brasileira', c1: '#ffd23c', c2: '#0a5c2e', c3: '#8dffb0', hours: 96, progress: 62, rating: 'L', installed: true, owned: true, price: 299.9, story: 'Brasileirões em campo. Vencer o Hexacampeonato.', character: 'NEYMAR BR', city: 'Estádio · Rio de Janeiro', music: 'pagode', control: 'fifa', missions: 12, mode: 'fifa' },
  { id: 'gow', title: 'GOD OF WAR BR', sub: 'Guerra nórdica no Brasil', c1: '#e8e2d8', c2: '#101820', c3: '#c9b38a', hours: 42, progress: 35, rating: '18+', installed: true, owned: true, price: 349.9, story: 'Kratos brasil é o último guerreiro. Caçar o titã.', character: 'KRATOS BR', city: 'Serra · neve', music: 'rock', control: 'gow', missions: 18, mode: 'gow' },
  { id: 'sm', title: 'SPIDER-MAN BR', sub: 'Teia urbana em São Paulo', c1: '#ff3b30', c2: '#3d0a24', c3: '#ff9d5c', hours: 54, progress: 41, rating: 'L', installed: true, owned: true, price: 299.9, story: 'Peter Parker pula o Burj no coração da cidade.', character: 'PETER BR', city: 'São Paulo · arranha-céu', music: 'hiphop', control: 'spiderman', missions: 15, mode: 'spiderman' },
  { id: 'ff', title: 'FREE FIRE BR', sub: 'Battle royale na ilha', c1: '#2dff8f', c2: '#062b1a', c3: '#b6ff5c', hours: 31, progress: 28, rating: '12+', installed: true, owned: true, price: 149.9, story: 'Soldado sobe na ilha. Ser o último em pé.', character: 'SOLDADO BR', city: 'Ilha · praia', music: 'funk', control: 'tiro', missions: 20, mode: 'battleroyale' },
  { id: 'mc', title: 'MINECRAFT BR', sub: 'Blocos · minerada · noite', c1: '#58c24a', c2: '#12331a', c3: '#a8e06b', hours: 88, progress: 47, rating: 'L', installed: true, owned: true, price: 249.9, story: 'Steve constrói a casa na serra. Creeper à noite.', character: 'STEVE BR', city: 'Serra · bloco', music: 'samba', control: 'sandbox', missions: 16, mode: 'sandbox' },
  { id: 'forza', title: 'FORZA BR', sub: '350 km/h nas ruas do Brasil', c1: '#28d17c', c2: '#062d36', c3: '#b6ff5c', hours: 19, progress: 28, rating: 'L', installed: false, owned: false, price: 179.9, story: 'Piloto brasileiro domina a pista de arrancar.', character: 'PILOTO BR', city: 'Pista · Contagem', music: 'rock', control: 'f1', missions: 10, mode: 'f1' },
  { id: 'tlou', title: 'THE LAST OF US BR', sub: 'Sobrevivência com o Joel BR', c1: '#9aa5b1', c2: '#0c1218', c3: '#7d9cb8', hours: 64, progress: 52, rating: '18+', installed: true, owned: true, price: 349.9, story: 'Joel e a filha escapam da infecção no sertão.', character: 'JOEL BR', city: 'Sertão · caatinga', music: 'trilha', control: 'survival', missions: 22, mode: 'survival' },
  { id: 'fn', title: 'FORTNITE BR', sub: 'Ilha colorida · dança e construção', c1: '#7a5cff', c2: '#1c0f4d', c3: '#4fd8ff', hours: 73, progress: 66, rating: '12+', installed: true, owned: true, price: 399.9, story: 'Dançarino brasil tira a vitória na ilha neon.', character: 'DANÇARINO BR', city: 'Ilha colorida', music: 'funk', control: 'battle', missions: 25, mode: 'battle' },
  { id: 'cod', title: 'CALL OF DUTY BR', sub: 'Operação sul-americana', c1: '#8fa3b8', c2: '#101820', c3: '#d7e6f2', hours: 112, progress: 71, rating: '18+', installed: true, owned: true, price: 349.9, story: 'Soldado BR enfrenta a opressão em campo e cidade.', character: 'SOLDADO BR', city: 'Campo · Heliponto', music: 'rock', control: 'tps', missions: 30, mode: 'tps' },
];
```

Hmm — ratings: original had numeric-ish strings like 'L'. Keep variety but GTA is '18+'. For others use sensible ratings: FIFA 'L', SM 'L', FF '12+', MC 'L', FORZA 'L', TLou '18+', FN '12+', CODBR '18+'.

Owned: only gta, futebol?, ... To make collection meaningful, set owned for the ones with installed true; not-owned for forza (buy). Keep flow: launchGame checks owned.

Now `launchGame`:

```js
  launchGame() {
    const g = GAMES[this.selectedGame];
    if (g.id !== 'gta' && !this.owned.has(g.id)) { this.openMenu('loja'); return; }
    this.currentGameId = g.id;
    this._saveLocal();
    this.audio.init();
    this.audio.cash();
    this.audio.speak(`Bem-vindo ao ${g.title}, edição ${g.character}. A aventura é sua.`);
    $('#ps5-layer').classList.add('off');
    document.body.classList.add('in-game');
    $('#game-ui').classList.remove('hidden');
    setTimeout(() => this.onPlay(this.profile), 380);
  }
```

Also `selectGame` sets currentGameId.

PS5System fields add:
```js
    this.currentGameId = 'gta';
    this.currentGame = GAMES[0];
    this.scale = { gameId: 'gta', level: 1 };
```
Persist scale in _saveLocal/_loadLocal.

`selectGame(index)`:
```js
  selectGame(index) {
    this.selectedGame = (index + GAMES.length) % GAMES.length;
    this.currentGameId = GAMES[this.selectedGame].id;
    this.currentGame = GAMES[this.selectedGame];
    this._layoutCarousel();
    this._updateGameInfo();
  }
```

`_updateGameInfo`: uses g; playGame button text: owned ? JOGAR : COMPRAR; dataset.mode.

Add scale button in dashboard info panel? The requirement: "Botão ESCALAR / AUMENTAR JOGO em cada jogo." Add to game info: a row with buttons NÍVEL 1/2/3? Or a button that cycles scale + scale bar. I'll add in `_updateGameInfo` a scale control:

```html
<div id="scaleRow" class="game-scale">
  <span>ESCALAR / AUMENTAR JOGO</span>
  <div class="scale-bar">
    <button data-scale="1">NÍVEL 1 · PEQUENO</button>
    <button data-scale="2">NÍVEL 2 · MÉDIO</button>
    <button data-scale="3">NÍVEL 3 · GIGANTÃO</button>
  </div>
</div>
```
And bind clicks → `this.scaleGame(+v)`.

`scaleGame(level)`:
```js
  scaleGame(level) {
    const g = this.currentGame;
    const max = this.weakPhone ? 2 : 3; // weak phone can't scale to giant
    const target = Math.max(1, Math.min(3, level));
    if (target > max) { this.toast('Não dá pra escalar para Gigantão no celular fraco, fica no Médio.'); target = max; }
