I see a critical bug in main.js:

```js
addEventListener('error', event => {
  if (!document.getElementById('fatal-error')) fatal(event.error || event.message);
});
```

This is wrong: it should check if fatal-error already exists before showing, i.e., only show for uncaught errors that aren't already handled. Actually the logic: if there's no fatal-error element, call fatal → which creates it. On subsequent errors it won't re-add, fine. But any uncaught error during gameplay would show the fatal overlay! That's aggressive but maybe intended... Actually it means any runtime error → fatal overlay → "Não foi possível iniciar o jogo". Hmm, this could be the source: if the perf HUD bug threw every frame... no, uncaught errors in RAF would trigger window error events? Actually errors in RAF callbacks do fire window.onerror. So after we introduced the updatePerfHUD bug, every frame error → fatal overlay appears (since first time it creates the box; afterwards `document.getElementById('fatal-error')` exists so it just calls fatal which reuses box... wait no, it calls fatal unconditionally when no box exists; if box exists it does nothing). OK so box stays, just updates detail.

Anyway, the error overlay is triggered both by startGame catch AND by window error listener. The window error listener might cause the overlay to appear for any uncaught error - including errors thrown in gameplay loops. That could be a source of the user's complaint. But more importantly, the user sees "Não foi possível iniciar o jogo" when clicking play.

Now, what error would be thrown for all games except GTA BR? Let's think about launch flow for other games... Actually maybe the error occurred BEFORE our perf edits, when launching a new game: e.g., `this.ps5.currentGame` etc.

Actually here's a likely candidate: In `launchGame`, for GTA we do certain things; for others we changed flow. Let me look at the current launchGame and how `startGame` is invoked.

Also important: `game.enter()` now does `const gDef = this.ps5?.currentGame;` — for the first game (gta) currentGame is set in constructor? In PS5System constructor we set `this.currentGame = GAMES[0];`. OK.

