Wait, there's a subtlety in my new setupKeyboard: I used `this.jump = true` etc. with arrow functions assigned to consts — `this` refers to the InputController instance since arrow functions capture `this`. Good.

But I also need to remove the old duplicate window blur listener in setup(): `window.addEventListener('blur', () => { this.keys = {}; ... })` — that's a different anonymous fn; should also be disposable. Let me update setup() to use addDisposable.

Current setup:
```js
  setup() {
    this.vc = document.getElementById('virtual-controls');
    this.setMode(this.mode, true);
    this.setupKeyboard();
    this.setupMouse();
    this.setupVirtual();
    this.setupGamepad();
    this.setupEditPanel();
    window.addEventListener('blur', () => { this.keys = {}; this.moveX = this.moveY = 0; });
  }
```
Replace last line with disposable version.

Then setupMouse: replace anonymous listeners with stored bound ones. The canvas is `document.getElementById('game-canvas')`. Since a new Game per launch creates a new InputController but the canvas element persists, listeners accumulate — must dispose. Let me rewrite setupMouse.

Current setupMouse (lines ~121-148):
```js
  setupMouse() {
    const canvas = document.getElementById('game-canvas');
    let lastX = 0, lastY = 0;
    canvas.addEventListener('pointerdown', e => {...});
    canvas.addEventListener('pointermove', e => {...});
    canvas.addEventListener('pointerup', e => {...});
    canvas.addEventListener('contextmenu', e => e.preventDefault());
    canvas.addEventListener('wheel', e => {...}, { passive: true });
    addEventListener('pointerup', () => { this.mouseDown = false; });
  }
```

Rewrite with bound handlers + disposables. Note pointermove uses closure vars lastX/lastY — fine with arrow.

